# Production Architecture

- Treat this project as a production data product, not a local script collection.
- Correctness, reproducibility, security, and operability take priority over delivery speed.
- Preserve immutable raw source data; clean and reinterpret data only downstream.
- Every source and output must define schema, grain, key, units, timezone, null policy, freshness, and owner.
- Pipeline retries must be idempotent and publication must be atomic.
- Do not commit credentials, use working secret defaults, or expose PII in logs and reports.
- Separate connectors, validation, transformations, metrics, reporting, and orchestration.
- CLI entry points delegate to testable domain functions and contain no metric logic.
- Reject unexpected schema drift and quarantine invalid records with explicit reason codes.
- Record run IDs, code/config versions, watermarks, row counts, quality results, and failures.
- Do not call a change production-ready without tests, observability, rollback, and staging verification.
- Keep architecture decisions and KPI behavior documented under `docs/`.
